+# Detection and switching benefit design
+
+The user authorized implementation and experiments on the collaborator delivery. Preserve the immutable delivery under LIMER_COLLAB_REVIEW_2026-10-28; modify only this working copy. Do not commit or push before user diff review and explicit authorization.
+
+## Objective
+Each registered eligible fault condition must achieve at least 95% correctly localized alarms strictly before 100 ms from injection. Count late, missed and failed attempts in the denominator. Severe delivery slowdown is eligible. Report per-condition results, unaffected-path false alarms, calibration assumptions, overhead, and confidence bounds separately.
+
+## Detection
+Keep legacy M13 as a matched baseline. Add periodic costed 64 KiB canary transfers on the same physical RDMA paths, with submission, ACK completion, actual sender retransmission, deadline observations, and active business ACK-prefix stagnation. A fixed 40 ms no-progress guard applies only to allocated, unconfirmed, unmigrated business work; idle work cannot trigger this signal. Learn and freeze a per-path healthy latency baseline during a fixed startup calibration interval; no fault timestamps, identities, loss parameters or future recovery state enter the detector. Replay the same pure rule independently in Python from raw events. Check weak loss, capacity reduction and blackhole, plus healthy, idle and bounded transient controls. Do not claim untested startup or arbitrary-network coverage.
+
+## Switching
+Preserve always-replace as a baseline. Add an observable sender/phase remaining-time estimate for staying versus replacement, incorporating owned work, flexible pending work, recent A/B ACK service, measured full candidate route time, FIFO coordination and final notification. Unknown candidate cost requires a paid probe. Require a positive conservative margin. Log all inputs and decisions, and audit the same pure policy independently. Both service-mode always and benefit policies pay identical 64 KiB full-route candidate probes; historical legacy mode retains its original 1024-byte liveness probe. Preserve existing epoch, prefix, physical resource, four-party coordination and final target completion checks.
+
+## Validation
+Use development cases to select parameters. Freeze code, binary, parameters and validation cases before the validation run. Use at least 60 independent seeds per registered fault condition and retain every attempt. Pair policies under identical workload, fault location, timing and seed. Include short task/transient fault, slow proxy and no-helper boundaries. Full native simulation is required; pure-function tests alone do not establish the research target.
